::SQL CHECK::
Which of the following is not true about the CHECK constraint?
{
    ~The CHECK constraint is used to limit the range value that can be placed in a column.
    =It prevents duplicate values from being entered into a column.
    ~It determines whether the value associated with the column is valid or not with the given criteria.
    ~It helps to check what type of values are to be stored in a table's column.
}


::SQL CHECK::
 The CHECK constraint helps maintain data integrity by preventing the insertion of incorrect or inappropriate data. {TRUE}
